{"qas": [
  {"question": "According to the UK AI Regulation White Paper, how does the government plan to use technical standards to support both assurance techniques and regulatory flexibility?", "answer": "The government plans to underpin assurance techniques with technical standards, which provide common understanding and flexibility by adapting to technological change.", "evidence": [{"page": 70, "quote": "Assurance techniques need to be underpinned by available technical standards, which provide common understanding across assurance providers."}, {"page": 71, "quote": "Technical standards can embed flexibility 158 into regulatory regimes and drive responsible innovation by helping organisations to address AI-related risks. 159"}]},
  {"question": "How does the UK AI Regulation White Paper propose to address capability gaps among regulators, and what collaborative options are mentioned?", "answer": "The White Paper suggests establishing a common pool of expertise and supporting collaborative initiatives like the DRCF to share skills and expertise among regulators.", "evidence": [{"page": 69, "quote": "It may, for example, be appropriate to establish a common pool of expertise that could establish best practice for supporting innovation through regulatory approaches and make it easier for regulators to work with each other on common issues. An alternative approach would be to explore and facilitate collaborative initiatives between regulators - including, where appropriate, further supporting existing initiatives such as the DRCF - to share skills and expertise."}]},
  {"question": "In the UK AI Regulation White Paper, what is the government's preferred initial model for the AI regulatory sandbox, and why?", "answer": "The government prefers the customised advice and support model for the sandbox, as it believes this delivers benefits most effectively in the short term.", "evidence": [{"page": 67, "quote": "Our current preference is for the customised advice and support model, as we think this is where we can deliver benefits most effectively in the short term."}]},
  {"question": "What is the role of the UK AI Standards Hub as described in the UK AI Regulation White Paper?", "answer": "The UK AI Standards Hub is established to champion the use of technical standards and support the development of an effective AI assurance ecosystem.", "evidence": [{"page": 70, "quote": "Government is already supporting the development of these tools by publishing a Roadmap to an effective AI assurance ecosystem in the UK 154 and establishing the UK AI Standards Hub 155 to champion the use of technical standards. 156"}]},
  {"question": "Which international forum did the UK announce funding for a Net Zero Data Space for AI Applications, and what was the purpose?", "answer": "At the 2022 GPAI Ministerial Summit in Japan, the UK announced £1.2m funding for a Net Zero Data Space to support Net Zero policy objectives.", "evidence": [{"page": 75, "quote": "At the 2022 GPAI Ministerial Summit in Japan, we demonstrated the scale of the UK's AI ambitions by announcing £1.2m of funding to develop a Net Zero Data Space for AI Applications (which will also support our Net Zero policy objectives). 167"}]},
  {"question": "According to the UK AI Regulation White Paper, what is one example of a technical standard for bias mitigation that regulators might promote?", "answer": "ISO/IEC TR 24027:2021 is cited as a bias mitigation standard that could be promoted by regulators like the FCA and EHRC.", "evidence": [{"page": 72, "quote": "Bias mitigation standards include ISO/IEC TR 24027:2021 and ISO/IEC AWI TS 12791*."}]}
]}
